FN-3 failure is a metadata visibility race after synchronous RDMA WRITE: peer bytes are written before PUT returns, but key index propagation over QP_HB can lag immediate TCP readback. The fix keeps readback mandatory and adds a bounded wait with samples.
  ✓ Read required state, reports, logs, and focused source files with bounded commands
  ✓ Diagnose FN-3 high-priority peer readback and implement a scoped fix
  → Verify function suite twice with SSH probes
  • Adjust RAID5 presentation handling and verify presentation performance path
  • Update pipeline state and create DONE or BLOCKED
